@cc ===========================================================================
@cc CHATKT:MODE - build the XMSG kernel loopback test.
@cc
@cc   @MODE CHATKT:MODE,,
@cc then          @CHATKT
@cc
@cc One small source, compiles in seconds. Needs XMP-B02:DEFS, XMP-B02:IMPT
@cc and XMP-100-1-B02:BRF under SYSTEM - the same COSMOS binding CHATSV uses.
@cc No CHATLIB, no MON-CALL, no VTM: this program talks only to the kernel.
@cc ===========================================================================

@cc --- clear the old build; NO SUCH FILE NAME on a first run is expected -----
@DELETE-FILE CHATKT:PROG
@DELETE-FILE CHATKT:BRF
@DELETE-FILE CHATKT:LIST

@cc --- compile to a real BRF; PROG-FILE NOT set, on purpose -------------------
@PLANC-100-F00
COMPILE CHATKT:PLNC,"CHATKT:LIST","CHATKT"
EXIT

@cc --- link: the PROGRAM first, then what satisfies it -----------------------
@BRF-LINKER-C01
PROGRAM-FILE "CHATKT"
LOAD CHATKT
LIBRARY-MODE ON
LOAD XMP-100-1-B02
LOAD PLANC-1BANK-F00
LIST-ENTRIES-UNDEFINED
EXIT

@cc ===========================================================================
@cc Built CHATKT:PROG. Run it with @CHATKT - needs XMSG up on this machine.
@cc
@cc Every line starts PASS or FAIL and the last line is a count. A FAIL in
@cc phase 3 alone means xmpfwri writes into the HELD arrival, not the fresh
@cc buffer xmpfget returned - the repeat-first-message bug, reproduced.
@cc
@cc CHECK THE LISTING for "*** ERROR" before believing any of it.
@cc ===========================================================================
